# === Secrets & environment ===
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# === Claude private / machine-local (NEVER pushed) ===
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# === Dependencies ===
node_modules/
.pnp.*

# === Build output ===
.next/
out/
dist/
build/

# === Logs ===
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
# ...but evidence bundles ARE committed proof (test-output.log included) — never ignore them.
!docs/evidence/**
# ADR-0055 moved evidence to initiatives/<lane>/evidence/ in lane-mode, and the negation
# above did not follow it — so the FIRST lane-scoped bundle silently lost its
# test-output.log to the *.log rule, and `verify` still passed because it reads the
# working directory rather than git. The rule was right; the path moved out from under it.
!initiatives/*/evidence/**

# === OS / editor junk ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# === Test / coverage ===
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Hook scratch state (PreCompact snapshots, graphify lock/log)
.claude/state/

# The same rule at ANY depth. `.claude/state/` above carries a middle separator, so git anchors
# it to the repo root only -- and memory's builder takes `--root <dir>`, so pointing it at a
# fixture tree under tests/ writes a derived index into a TRACKED directory that the line above
# does not cover. Verified with `git check-ignore` in Cycle 11: it did not match.
**/.claude/state/

# arc-registry.json is a per-INSTALL artifact written into consumer targets, never the mold
# itself (Phase 02, REQ-08). It's excluded from the golden + tree-diff gates by design, so
# ignore it here too — a stray one can never be silently committed into the mold's .claude/.
.claude/arc-registry.json

# Hook write-probes (freeze-check / edit-guard test their write access) — never commit
.writetest*
**/.writetest
*.wt
**/.wt

# Graphify: fully local + regenerable, and holds machine-specific paths (.graphify_root,
# .graphify_python) — never commit any of it. It does NOT rebuild itself here: the global
# auto-update hook is GSD-gated on .planning/config.json, which arc has not got, so this index
# is only ever as fresh as the last manual `graphify update .` (checked 2026-08-22).
graphify-out/

# CodeGraph: local SQLite symbol/edge index (.codegraph/codegraph.db, ~14MB, machine-local
# and regenerable via `codegraph init .`). Ignoring the whole directory keeps its own stray
# .gitignore out of the tree too.
.codegraph/

# Codex
.codex
.agents
AGENTS.md

# Planner-bench output (large, regenerable — not committed despite the evidence rule above)
docs/evidence/planner-bench/
.gstack/

# Same-device temp dirs used by the policy filesystem-identity tests (hardlinks cannot
# cross devices, and the CI runners split the checkout and the temp dir across volumes).
# Each test removes its own in a finally block; this is the belt for a crashed run.
.pol-tmp-*/
tmp-escape-probe/
